task: queue-swap
agent: opus5-intent
started: 2026-09-09
branch: feature/queue-swap
worktree: ../okay-wt-queueswap

why: the operator picked this group (2026-09-08) as the next one. It
  is also the only entry left whose premise TODAY'S measurements
  partly contradict, so it gets measured before it gets built.

what the entry proposes: move the ring -> partitioned swap out of the
  `Growing` wrapper and into `SentinelChannel`, which holds the buffer
  in a volatile field and REPLACES it, so there is exactly one layer
  on each side of the swap instead of two. Six steps are filed:
  volatile field + `growingTo(parts)`, waiter queues sized for the
  grown part count up front, the swap as one CAS with losers using the
  winner's buffer, `wakeAllSenders()` right after, the every-64th-push
  sample as the trigger, and controls that must not move.

DISQUALIFYING EVIDENCE, registered before any work:

  The entry's whole prize is "the layer `Growing` still pays". On
  2026-09-08 that layer was priced and it is two separate things:

  1. THE FORWARDING DISPATCH — a buffer that only forwards measured
     **1.02x** the ring it forwards to. Free. This is the only half
     the channel-level swap actually removes.
  2. `sample()` — a counter write on every push plus an every-64th
     thread compare. This is where the residual cost is, and it does
     NOT move: the channel-level version needs the same trigger, so
     it pays the same sample.

  So the proposal as filed buys at most 2%, and the thing worth
  attacking is the trigger, not the layer.

  THE TEST, taken first and before any code: at ONE producer and
  equal capacity, a clean alternating A/B of the channel on `growing`
  against the channel on a plain `Ring`. `docs/queues.md` reads 183
  against 169 (8%) from the buffer table; the channel-level number is
  the one that decides this entry.

    - gap at or under the noise floor (5.9% p95 on uncontended lanes)
      -> the entry is REFUTED as filed. `growing` is already the
      default channel buffer (2026-09-08), the layer is already free,
      and there is nothing left for a swap to buy. It closes as
      done-by-other-means with the measurement written down.
    - gap real and it is the DISPATCH -> build the six steps.
    - gap real and it is `sample()` -> the six steps are the wrong
      work. Make the trigger free at one producer instead, and say so
      in the entry.

predict: the gap is real (~8%) and it is `sample()`, not the layer —
  which refutes the filed plan and redirects the lane to the trigger.
  Recorded so that being wrong is visible.
